{
  "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
  "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in case 06-6330, Kimbrough versus United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Could the Congress have mandated the result and the rationale that the Fourth Circuit used here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But -- and I take it your submission is that the district court must be able to make the determination that the commission's policy is to be disregarded in every case to come before the court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Your Honor, 3553(a) requires individualized sentencing. There's no question that judges are required to follow in every case the mandates of 3553(a) and to calculate the advisory Guidelines correctly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: And Mr. Nachmanoff, I think that you are agreeing, although you don't want to come right out and say it, with Justice Scalia's point; that is, anything from a hundred to one down to one to one is open to the district judge; and within that range, there is no abuse of discretion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question in this case is essentially, can a district court reasonably disagree with the judgment of Congress concerning the ratio between the quantity-based sentences for crack and powder."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Dreeben, can I ask a question right at the outset that is critical for me. I think this case may well be controlled by the decision in Neal against the United States, which is not cited in the government brief and wasn't cited in the blue brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Isn't your answer also to Justice Breyer's question the post-Neal amendment to the statute which in effect says, you know, make your Guidelines consistent with the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: I was -- and correct me if I'm wrong. I was under the impression that 80 percent of the sentences that are actually imposed are at the mandatory minimum."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: You have a conflict in the statute. One says await the guideline. Another says avoid unwarranted disparities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: Our position here, I think, is consistent with our view that you read statutes both for what they say and for what they mean."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: If Congress passes a statute that says the mandatory minimum sentence of eight years for possessing a 12-inch shotgun unlawfully, does that mean it wants four years for a 6-inch shotgun?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Congress has legislated in this area after Booker. They have not imposed the 100 to 1 ratio throughout the -- other than as a mandatory minimum and maximum."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: I'm not aware that they have legislated in this area after Booker, Mr. Chief Justice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: It is done in a logically proportional manner --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Nachmanoff",
      "case_id": "2007-06-6330",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c25a732096714a4fc0fc7db2225f67e7426ab35201261b3d1d971f711b6da5ed",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c25a73209671-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. NACHMANOFF: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. If I can respond, Justice Stevens, I think -- you asked about the percentage of cases in crack that are at the mandatory minimum or near it. I would point the Court to page 33, footnote 10 of our opening brief. It is approximately 70 percent or just over that that hit at the mandatory minimum or just one or two levels above that."
    },
    {
